BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Legacy in Sound: Featuring the Next Generation of Music Educators 
 and Performers
DTSTART:20261112T000000Z
DTEND:20261112T045959Z
DTSTAMP:20261110T170003Z
UID:3150ba01c748c7b8847a8ee6cf75e943c1e54150@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Music
DESCRIPTION:Join us for our on-campus preview concert of our upcoming perf
 ormance at Lincoln Center's Alice Tully Hall!\nThe concert highlights Itha
 ca College’s long tradition of preparing outstanding musicians\, educato
 rs\, and arts leaders through rigorous training and transformative perform
 ance experiences. Whether pursuing careers as performers\, teachers\, scho
 lars\, or creative professionals\, students carry these experiences into t
 he ensembles\, classrooms\, and communities they will serve throughout the
 ir lives.\n“Legacy in Sound: Featuring the Next Generation of Music Educ
 ators and Performers” will feature the Ithaca College Wind Ensemble\, di
 rected by Daniel Cook\; Jazz Ensemble\, directed by Mike Titlebaum\; Symph
 ony Orchestra\, conducted by Ho-Yin Kwok\; and Choir\, directed by Khyle W
 ooten.\nProgram highlights will include a commissioned work by composer an
 d Ithaca College professor emeritus Dana Wilson\, performed by the Jazz En
 semble and Wind Ensemble\; Adolphus Hailstork’s Shout for Joy\, performe
 d by the Choir\; and the final movement of Beethoven’s Symphony No. 9\, 
 bringing together the Symphony Orchestra and Choir. The Jazz Ensemble will
  also perform selections by Les Brown and Steve Brown.\nReserve your FREE 
 tickets here:\nhttps://www.purplepass.com/events/385572-preview-concert-fo
 r-alice-tully-hall-lincoln-center-nov-11th-2026\n\nSource: FLXcalendar - h
 ttps://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78503471/20261111190000
GEO:42.421022;-76.495805
LOCATION:Ford Hall at Ithaca College\, 146 Conservatory Drive\, Ithaca\, N
 ew York\, 14850\, United States
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78503471/20261111190000
END:VEVENT
