DESCRIPTION:Event by Community Arts of Elmira\nCommunity Arts of Elmira\nD
 uration: 1 hr 30 min\nPublic\nSave-the-Date for "Wreathe Bingo" An Older A
 dult/Caregiver Free Arts Wellness Event!\nThe Third "Learn\, Explore\, Cre
 ate\, Connect (LECC): An Interactive Wellness Event for Older Adults and C
 aregivers" takes place Wednesday/November 18\, 2026\, 1:30-3:00pm. Registe
 r at 607-737-5520/Chemung County Department of Aging and Long Term Care.\n
 People not only will play "Wreath Bingo" for the chance to take home a har
 dy plant\, but also have the opportunity to paint holiday ornaments with A
 rtist Jennifer Sekella to enhance what plants they might already have at h
 ome! LECC is a wellness open house offering access to essential\, best-car
 e resources in a supportive environment for all participants\, who can eng
 age with professionals from the host organizations onsite to learn and ask
  questions\, while making new connections with people facing similar life 
 challenges and searching for help.\nThank you to Artist Filomena Jack of F
 ilomena Jack Studion for creating this flier.\nHosted by the Alzheimer's A
 ssociation\, Chemung County Department of Aging and Long Term Care and Com
 munity Arts of Elmira!\nLocation: Community Arts of Elmira\, 413 Lake Stre
