DESCRIPTION:The African Drumming and Dance Ensemble will be joined by the 
 first-year seminar class to perform several pieces from West Africa\, main
 ly Ghana. Students have been learning about the traditional music and cult
 ural practices of several Ghanaian ethnic groups\, including the Ewe\, Ga
 \, Ashanti\, and Dagomba.\nThrough this experience\, students are learning
  to process and perform music orally\, embracing the traditional methods t
 hrough which these musical practices have been passed down from generation
  to generation. Just as importantly\, they are developing a deeper respect
  and appreciation for the musicians\, cultural practitioners\, and ancesto
 rs whose musical legacies have been preserved and shared with others acros
 s the world.\nWe offer our heartfelt gratitude to those ancestors who have
  made it possible for us to learn from\, experience\, and celebrate these 
 rich musical traditions. To them\, we say\, “Ahsay!”\nReserve your FRE
 E tickets here:\nhttps://www.purplepass.com/events/381324-west-african-dru
 mming-and-dance-nov-19th-2026\n\nSource: FLXcalendar - https://calendar.ti
