BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Famed Astrophysicist Neil deGrasse Tyson - 2027 Walter R. Smith Vi
 siting Scholar Lecture at Corning Museum of Glass
DTSTART:20270430T230000Z
DTEND:20270501T035959Z
DTSTAMP:20261110T170003Z
UID:72b9467ed33d702b22265ef4ef4918946f8e07b6@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Science,Connection,BIPOC
DESCRIPTION:SUNY Corning Community College (SUNY CCC) and Corning Incorpor
 ated are proud to announce renowned astrophysicist\, author\, and science 
 communicator Dr. Neil deGrasse Tyson as the featured speaker for the 2027 
 Walter R. Smith Visiting Scholar Series\, which brings world-class thinker
 s\, leaders\, and innovators to the region to engage students and communit
 y members in meaningful dialogue.\nThe event will take place on Friday\, A
 pril 30\, 2027\, at 7:00 p.m.\, at the Corning Museum of Glass auditorium.
  Admission is free and open to the public on a first-come\, first-served b
 asis.\n“Bringing Dr. Neil deGrasse Tyson to our region is an extraordina
 ry opportunity to explore the big questions that shape our understanding o
 f the universe\, and we are especially grateful to Corning Incorporated fo
 r helping make this event possible\,” said Dr. Terence Finley\, Presiden
 t of SUNY Corning Community College. “At SUNY CCC\, we believe where you
  start matters\, and we are committed to creating experiences that broaden
  perspectives and open doors for our students and community. We are proud 
 to welcome Dr. Tyson through the Walter R. Smith Visiting Scholar Series t
 o share the wonder and possibility that define the Corning Community Colle
 ge spirit.”\n“Corning Incorporated is thrilled to co-sponsor the Walte
 r R. Smith Visiting Scholar Series and welcome Dr. Neil deGrasse Tyson to 
 the Southern Tier\,” said Dr. Millicent K. Ruffin\, Division Vice Presid
 ent\, Corning Community Impact. “Dr. Tyson brings complex ideas to life 
 and sparks curiosity across generations\, offering a special opportunity f
 or our community\, particularly young people beginning to imagine what the
 ir futures might hold. We are grateful for these partnerships that create 
 meaningful experiences in the places we call home.”\nDr. Tyson is a worl
 d-renowned astrophysicist\, author\, and science communicator. He serves a
 s director of the Hayden Planetarium at the American Museum of Natural His
 tory and is a research associate in the Museum’s Department of Astrophys
 ics. A graduate of Harvard University and Columbia University\, he is the 
 author of numerous New York Times bestselling books\, including Astrophysi
 cs for People in a Hurry\, and served as executive science editor\, host\,
  and narrator of Cosmos: A Spacetime Odyssey. His contributions to science
  and public engagement have earned him 27 honorary doctorates\, NASA’s D
 istinguished Public Service Medal\, and appointments to national space pol
 icy commissions and NASA’s Advisory Council.\nFor more information regar
 ding the 2027 Walter R. Smith Visiting Scholar Series\, please visit the V
 isiting Scholar Series page.\n\nSource: FLXcalendar - https://calendar.tim
 e.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78507375/20270430190000
GEO:42.1498;77.0542
LOCATION:Corning Museum of Glass\, One Museum Way\, Corning\, NY\, 14830
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78507375/20270430190000
END:VEVENT
